    {
      "id": "302eabb8f7a84e6c997f80ad2dfc1b39",
      "title": "Opportunity Zones of Alaska",
      "url": "https://storymaps.arcgis.com/stories/302eabb8f7a84e6c997f80ad2dfc1b39",
      "publisher": "DCRAOpenData",
      "status": "needs_review",
      "publisher_verified": false,
      "native_geography": null,
      "production_admission": false,
      "properties": {
        "snippet": "Explore economic details of the Qualified Opportunity Zones in Alaska. Qualified Opportunity Zones (QOZ) are areas and communities that have been identified as economically distressed. \nOpportunity Zones 2.0 are currently in vetting status. Written Comment Period: April 1- April 30, 2026. Interested parties may also submit written comments to the department April 1 through April 30, 2026. All comments should be emailed to emily.fairbanks@alaska.gov.",
        "extent": null,
        "commentsEnabled": true,
        "groupDesignations": null,
        "access": "public",
        "apiToken2ExpirationDate": -1,
        "typeKeywords": [
          "arcgis-storymaps",
          "smdraftresourceid:draft_1776462251224.json",
          "smfirstpublisheddate:1607470483605",
          "smpublisheddate:1776462251224",
          "smstatuspublished",
          "smversiondraft:26.13.1229",
          "smversionpublished:26.13.1229",
          "StoryMap",
          "Web Application"
        ],
        "description": "<p>Qualified Opportunity Zones (QOZ) are areas and communities that have been identified as economically distressed. New investments in these communities, under certain conditions, may be eligible for preferential tax treatment. They were established in the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017 as a means to increase investment in lower income areas.</p><p><span style='background-color:rgb(255,255,255); color:rgb(48,78,78); font-family:&quot;Noto Serif&quot;, serif; font-size:19.2px;'><span style='display:inline !important; float:none; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>Qualified Opportunity Zones were nominated and approved by the Secretary of U.S. Treasury. In Alaska, there were 25 census tracts identified. Due to the large geography of Alaska, some tracts are equivalent to organized boroughs, such as the Northwest Arctic Borough, while others are smaller areas within a borough as is the case with the Municipality of Anchorage.</span></span></p><p>Opportunity Zones 2.0 are currently in vetting status. Written Comment Period: April 1- April 30, 2026. Interested parties may also submit written comments to the department April 1 through April 30, 2026. All comments should be emailed to emily.fairbanks@alaska.gov.<br />&nbsp;</p>",
        "licenseInfo": "<p style='margin:2.0pt 0in;'><strong>DISCLAIMER:</strong>&nbsp;The Division of Community and Regional Affairs (DCRA) provides the Community Database Online (CDO) as a source of information to aid in advising and assisting local governments, including for research purposes. DCRA is not a referral agency and cannot make specific recommendations or endorsements. Links to other agencies and related organizations are provided as a service, and do not constitute endorsement or recommendations for the agencies/organizations or websites.&nbsp;</p><p style='margin:2.0pt 0in;'><span style='font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; font-size:12.0pt;'>&nbsp;</span></p><p style='margin-bottom:.0001pt;'><span style='font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; font-size:12.0pt;'><strong>Please note:</strong>&nbsp;In an effort to uphold information data integrity in the CDO we always welcome and appreciate your help and review of your community's data. If you encounter any incorrect information, please send an e-mail to:&nbsp;</span><a href='mailto:DCRAResearchAndAnalysis@alaska.gov' rel='nofollow ugc'><span style='color:blue; font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; font-size:12.0pt;'><u>DCRA Research and Analysis</u></span></a></p>",
